    "summary": "High‑energy set with smoking Truckin' and fiery China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The show bursts with a scorching Truckin' and a searing China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider transition, while Keith Godchaux delivers his best Beat It On Down The Line solo. Loose Lucy and the Wharf Rat > Stella Blue pairing shine in the second set, and the crowd’s enthusiasm fuels an uninterrupted high‑energy flow throughout.",
    "review": "October 27, 1973 at the Indianapolis State Fair Coliseum finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. From the opening of The Promised Land the band rolls forward with tight grooves, but it’s the mid‑set fireworks that define this night – Jerry’s lead lines blaze through Truckin', and the China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue feels like a volcanic eruption of melody and rhythm. Keith Godchaux is on fire, especially on his soaring Beat It On Down The Line solo that many fans rank among his finest. The second set maintains the momentum with a country‑rock swagger; Loose Lucy grooves with playful verve while Wharf Rat flows seamlessly into Stella Blue, delivering both lyrical depth and jam‑centric excitement. The audience’s energy never wanes, making this performance one of the standout 1973 recordings for anyone chasing that classic early‑70s Dead magic.",
